she was someone who was loved by  everyone who worked with and liked by  everyone who worked with and admired  an emotional alec baldwin visibly shaken  during an interview with abc news's  george stephanopoulos  their conversation will air in full on  thursday december 2nd but on wednesday  the network released a clip of what's to  come you haven't said much in public  since that tragic accident why speak out  now i think the big question  and the one you must have asked yourself  a thousand times  how could this have happened it's the  actor's first sit down since the october  tragedy on the set of rust when baldwin  reportedly fired a prop gun that  accidentally killed cinematographer  helena hutchins and wounded director  joel souza an investigation into the  shooting is ongoing during the interview  baldwin denies claims that he pulled the  trigger that fired the fatal shot it  wasn't in the script for the trigger to  be pulled well the trigger wasn't pulled  i didn't pull the trigger so you never  pulled the trigger no no no no i would  never point a gun at anyone and pull a  trigger at them never what did you think  happened the actor raises questions  about how the live bullet got on the set  in the first place how did a real bullet  get on that set i have no idea someone  put a live bullet in a gun a bullet that  wasn't even supposed to be on the  property he also reflects on what he  could have done differently to prevent  the accident that ended in tragedy you  said you're not a victim but is this the  worst thing that's ever happened to you  yes  yep  yeah  because i  i think back  and i think of what could i have done  in the meantime e.t has obtained new  documents that shed light on what  happened on set that day an affidavit  claims the film's armorer hannah  gutierrez reid told investigators that  the weapon was checked on set but that  she quote didn't really check it too  much  gutierrez reid also may have put blame  on baldwin the document claiming that  the armorer said quote they weren't even  supposed to be pulling the hammer back  but back to baldwin's interview on  wednesday's good morning america  stephanopoulos who co-anchors the show  opened up about what it was like having  such an emotional conversation with the  actor i've done thousands of interviews  in the last 20 years at abc this was the  most  intense i've ever experienced he was  also very candid he was very forthcoming  he answered every question he talked  about helena hutchins talked about  meeting with her family as well went  through in detail  what happened on the set that day and i  have to tell you i was surprised  [Music]
 

